{#
  Homepage audit form — posts to modules/leadgenerator/controllers/AuditController.
  Standard POST + redirect, no JS required. Repopulates from the flashed values on a
  validation error, exactly as the contact form does.

  IT BORROWS c-form WHOLESALE rather than bringing its own styling. The two forms do the
  same job and there is nothing yet to say they should look different; a second set of
  classes would be a second thing to keep in step for no answered question. If this ever
  needs its own look it gets a modifier, not a copy.

  THE URL IS ASKED FOR FIRST, and that is a decision about conversion rather than markup.
  Somebody who has typed their domain and watched something start is likelier to give an
  address than somebody asked for one up front. It also sidesteps the trap in checking a
  URL before accepting the lead: a prospect whose site refuses our crawler would see an
  error and leave, and their address would go with them. So this accepts, queues, and lets
  a failure become an entry a human looks at.
#}
{# The id the redirect lands on and the id on the rendered state. Named once: two
   spellings of it is a form that posts and a page that ignores where it was told to go. #}
{% set anchor = 'link' %}

{# THE THANK-YOU COPY, from the tool's own entry, with the original wording as the
   fallback while the fields are empty — the same shape _components/form.twig uses for the
   contact single. Both fields were already on the `audit` entry type and neither was ever
   read, so editing them in the control panel changed nothing.

   FETCHED HERE RATHER THAN PASSED IN, because this component is included with
   `with_context = false` on purpose: a form that read whatever happened to be in scope
   would work on this page and break in the next caller. It asks for the entry it means by
   section and type, which is the same question modules\leadgenerator\audit\services\Audit
   asks for the tool's name. #}
{% set tool = craft.entries().section('tools').type('audit').status(null).one() %}
{% set sentTitle = (tool.messageSentTitle ?? '')|trim ?: 'Measuring your homepage' %}
{% set sentText = (tool.messageSentText ?? '')|trim
    ?: 'It takes a few minutes — we photograph the whole page, not just the first screen. The report lands in your inbox when it is ready.' %}

{% set old = craft.app.session.getFlash('auditForm') ?? {} %}
{% set error = craft.app.session.getFlash('error') %}
{% set fieldErrors = craft.app.session.getFlash('auditErrors') ?? {} %}

{% macro errorMessage(message) %}
    <span class="c-form__error" role="alert">{{ message }}</span>
{% endmacro %}

{# Inlined rather than the icon() sprite so its currentColor takes the red set in CSS —
   same reason as the contact form's. #}
{% macro errorIcon() %}
    <svg class="c-form__input-icon" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" fill="none"
        viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="1.5" stroke="currentColor" aria-hidden="true">
        <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"
            d="M12 9v3.75m9-.75a9 9 0 1 1-18 0 9 9 0 0 1 18 0Zm-9 3.75h.008v.008H12v-.008Z" />
    </svg>
{% endmacro %}
{% import _self as f %}

{% if craft.app.session.get('auditSubmitted') %}
    {# THE WAIT IS STATED, because it is minutes rather than seconds and nothing about a
       submitted form shows that. A person told "shortly" refreshes; a person told what is
       happening does not. #}
    <div class="c-form c-form--done" id="{{ anchor }}" role="status" tabindex="-1">
        <p class="c-form__thanks">{{ sentTitle }}</p>
        <p class="c-form__thanks-sub">{{ sentText }}</p>
    </div>
{% elseif craft.app.session.getFlash('auditBlocked') %}
    {# Rate limited or filled implausibly fast. A one-time notice rather than a banner they
       can retry against, and deliberately not an explanation of which rule they tripped. #}
    <div class="c-form c-form--done" id="{{ anchor }}" role="status" tabindex="-1">
        <p class="c-form__thanks">Not submitted</p>
        <p class="c-form__thanks-sub">Please get in touch directly and I will run it for you</p>
    </div>
{% else %}
<form class="c-form" method="post" accept-charset="UTF-8" id="{{ anchor }}" data-audit-form>
    {{ csrfInput() }}
    {# A VIP visitor already has their details on their entry (modules/jonson/services/Vip),
       so they are not asked twice. A failed submit's own values always win: what somebody
       typed is what they meant, even where it differs from what we hold. #}
    {% set vip = craft.app.getModule('jonson').vip.current() %}
    <input type="hidden" name="action" value="leadgenerator/audit/submit">
    {# BACK TO THE FORM, NOT THE TOP OF THE PAGE. A plain POST + redirect reloads at the top,
       and this form sits a long way down a landing page — on /tools/homepage-analysis the
       visitor lands 5,000px above the message telling them their report is coming, and
       every sign of having submitted anything is off screen.

       A fragment on the redirect is all it takes, and it costs no JavaScript: the browser
       is told where to land. The id is on whichever state renders — the form, the thanks,
       or the blocked notice — and only one of them is ever on the page at a time, so they
       can share it. #}
    {{ redirectInput(craft.app.request.pathInfo ~ '#' ~ anchor) }}

    {# Signed render time — the controller refuses a form completed implausibly fast.
       Hashed, so the client's clock and the client's honesty are both beside the point. #}
    <input type="hidden" name="ts" value="{{ craft.app.security.hashData(now|date('U')) }}">
    {# The page this was sent from. Kept only when it is one of ours — see
       FormGuard::ownReferrer. #}
    <input type="hidden" name="referrerUrl" value="{{ craft.app.request.absoluteUrl }}">

    {# Honeypot — hidden from people, tempting to bots. A filled one succeeds silently. #}
    <div class="c-form__hp" aria-hidden="true">
        <label>Leave this blank
            <input type="text" name="website" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off">
        </label>
    </div>

    {% if error %}
        <p class="c-form__flash c-form__flash--error" role="alert">{{ error }}</p>
    {% endif %}

    <label class="c-form__field{{ fieldErrors.auditUrl is defined ? ' c-form__field--error' }}">
        <span class="c-form__label">
            <span class="c-form__label-text">Your Homepage URL</span>
            {% if fieldErrors.auditUrl is defined %}{{ f.errorMessage(fieldErrors.auditUrl) }}{% endif %}
        </span>
        <span class="c-form__control">
            {# `type="url"` is deliberately NOT used: it demands a scheme, and nobody types
               one. The controller adds https to a bare domain and refuses anything that is
               not http(s), which is the check that actually matters. #}
            <input class="c-form__input" type="text" name="auditUrl" inputmode="url"
                autocomplete="url" autocapitalize="off" autocorrect="off" spellcheck="false"
                value="{{ old.auditUrl ?? '' }}" placeholder="example.com" required>
            {% if fieldErrors.auditUrl is defined %}{{ f.errorIcon() }}{% endif %}
        </span>
    </label>

    {# OPTIONAL, AND THAT IS THE POINT OF IT. A lead with nobody in mind still converts;
       one who names a rival has told you what they are actually worried about, which is
       worth more than the field costs. Filled in, it adds a second set of pages to the same
       PDF and a comparison at the end. #}
    <label class="c-form__field{{ fieldErrors.auditCompetitorUrl is defined ? ' c-form__field--error' }}">
        <span class="c-form__label">
            <span class="c-form__label-text">Competitor Homepage URL
                <span class="c-form__optional">(optional)</span></span>
            {% if fieldErrors.auditCompetitorUrl is defined %}{{ f.errorMessage(fieldErrors.auditCompetitorUrl) }}{% endif %}
        </span>
        <span class="c-form__control">
            <input class="c-form__input" type="text" name="auditCompetitorUrl" inputmode="url"
                autocomplete="off" autocapitalize="off" autocorrect="off" spellcheck="false"
                value="{{ old.auditCompetitorUrl ?? '' }}" placeholder="example.com">
            {% if fieldErrors.auditCompetitorUrl is defined %}{{ f.errorIcon() }}{% endif %}
        </span>
    </label>

    <div class="c-form__row">
        <label class="c-form__field{{ fieldErrors.firstName is defined ? ' c-form__field--error' }}">
            <span class="c-form__label">
                <span class="c-form__label-text">First Name</span>
                {% if fieldErrors.firstName is defined %}{{ f.errorMessage(fieldErrors.firstName) }}{% endif %}
            </span>
            <span class="c-form__control">
                <input class="c-form__input" type="text" name="firstName" autocomplete="given-name"
                    value="{{ old.firstName ?? vip.firstName ?? '' }}" placeholder="Henri" required>
                {% if fieldErrors.firstName is defined %}{{ f.errorIcon() }}{% endif %}
            </span>
        </label>
        <label class="c-form__field{{ fieldErrors.surname is defined ? ' c-form__field--error' }}">
            <span class="c-form__label">
                <span class="c-form__label-text">Surname</span>
                {% if fieldErrors.surname is defined %}{{ f.errorMessage(fieldErrors.surname) }}{% endif %}
            </span>
            <span class="c-form__control">
                <input class="c-form__input" type="text" name="surname" autocomplete="family-name"
                    value="{{ old.surname ?? vip.surname ?? '' }}" placeholder="Cartier-Bresson" required>
                {% if fieldErrors.surname is defined %}{{ f.errorIcon() }}{% endif %}
            </span>
        </label>
    </div>

    <label class="c-form__field{{ fieldErrors.email is defined ? ' c-form__field--error' }}">
        <span class="c-form__label">
            <span class="c-form__label-text">Email</span>
            {% if fieldErrors.email is defined %}{{ f.errorMessage(fieldErrors.email) }}{% endif %}
        </span>
        <span class="c-form__control">
            <input class="c-form__input" type="email" name="email" autocomplete="email"
                value="{{ old.email ?? vip.email ?? '' }}" placeholder="thedecisivemoment@example.com" required>
            {% if fieldErrors.email is defined %}{{ f.errorIcon() }}{% endif %}
        </span>
    </label>

    {% include '_components/button.twig' with { label: 'Send', type: 'submit', size: 'sm' } only %}
</form>
{% endif %}
